          {
            "title": "Find the risky operation",
            "id": 152111,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Invalid quantity text may raise <code>ValueError</code>. Which operation should a focused <code>try</code> block protect from that expected failure?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"order_import.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Importing&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"quantity = int(form[\" /><text value=\"&quot;quantity&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"])\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"save_order(form, quantity)\" /></content></code><selection multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Converting <code>form[\"quantity\"]</code> with <code>int()</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Displaying the import message</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">Saving the completed order</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Converting <code>form[\"quantity\"]</code> with <code>int()</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Saving can also raise <code>ValueError</code>, but only invalid quantity text should trigger a quantity warning. What belongs in that <code>try</code>?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"order_import.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Importing&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"quantity = int(form[\" /><text value=\"&quot;quantity&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"])\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"save_order(form, quantity)\" /></content></code><selection multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Only converting form[\"quantity\"] with int().</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">The conversion and save_order() together.</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">Only save_order().</item><item value=\"4\" correct=\"false\">All three lines, so any ValueError produces the quantity warning.</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Only converting form[\"quantity\"] with int().</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Keep the try block narrow",
            "id": 152112,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Complete the focused block around the quantity conversion.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"order_import.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"process\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(form)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  print(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Importing&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"try\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    quantity = int(form[\" /><text value=\"&quot;quantity&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"])\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"except\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" ValueError:\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"None\" class=\"literal\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" quantity\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" isDefault=\"true\" startIndex=\"42\" endIndex=\"45\" /></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to type <code>try</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Catch the expected error",
            "id": 152113,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Catch only the error expected from invalid numeric text.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"seat_parser.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"parse_seats\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(value)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"try\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" int(value)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"except\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" ValueError:\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"None\" class=\"literal\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"62\" endIndex=\"72\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"KeyError\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>ValueError</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Catch only invalid numeric text and return a failure value without inventing a seat count.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"seat_parser.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"parse_seats\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(value)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"try\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" int(value)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"except\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" ValueError:\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"None\" class=\"literal\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"62\" endIndex=\"72\" /><option startIndex=\"85\" endIndex=\"89\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"KeyError\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"Exception\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"0\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>ValueError</code>, followed by <code>None</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Choose the recovery point",
            "id": 152114,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p><code>parse_port()</code> converts text. <code>start_server()</code> can cancel startup and show a useful message. Where should <code>ValueError</code> be caught?</p><selection multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Inside <code>start_server()</code>, around the call to <code>parse_port()</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Inside <code>parse_port()</code>, before calling <code>int()</code></item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">Inside the built-in <code>int()</code> function</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Inside <code>start_server()</code>, around the call to <code>parse_port()</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Two callers use <code>parse_port()</code>, but only <code>start_server()</code> can cancel startup. Where should startup recovery go?</p><selection multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Catch ValueError in start_server() around its call to parse_port().</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Catch it in parse_port() and always return 0 to every caller.</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">Catch it in both functions, with parse_port() returning 0 first.</item><item value=\"4\" correct=\"false\">Catch it after the parse_port() call has already completed.</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Catch ValueError in start_server() around its call to parse_port().</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Keep other work visible",
            "id": 152115,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Which parts of the code should be moved outside the <code>try</code> block to make the error handling more targeted?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"order_import.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"try\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  quantity = int(order[\" /><text value=\"&quot;quantity&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"])\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  total = quantity * order[\" /><text value=\"&quot;price&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  save_order(total)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"except\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" ValueError:\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  print(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Invalid quantity&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /></content></code><selection multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">The total calculation and <code>save_order()</code> call</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">The quantity conversion</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">Every line in the function</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">The total calculation and <code>save_order()</code> call.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>The quantity is valid, but <code>save_order()</code> raises <code>ValueError</code>. Only quantity failures should print the warning. What should move out?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"order_import.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"try\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  quantity = int(order[\" /><text value=\"&quot;quantity&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"])\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  total = quantity * order[\" /><text value=\"&quot;price&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  save_order(total)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"except\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" ValueError:\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  print(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Invalid quantity&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /></content></code><selection multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">The total calculation and save_order() call.</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">The quantity conversion alone.</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">Only the total calculation; keep save_order() protected.</item><item value=\"4\" correct=\"false\">Nothing; matching exception types always need the same response.</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">The total calculation and save_order() call.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Handle a missing key",
            "id": 152116,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Complete the first specific handler for a missing quantity key.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"order_import.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"parse_quantity\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(order)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"try\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" int(order[\" /><text value=\"&quot;quantity&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"])\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"except\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" KeyError:\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"&quot;Missing quantity&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"except\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" ValueError:\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"&quot;Invalid quantity&quot;\" class=\"string\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"77\" endIndex=\"85\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"ValueError\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>KeyError</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Return separate messages for a missing quantity key and invalid integer text.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"order_import.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"parse_quantity\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(order)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"try\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" int(order[\" /><text value=\"&quot;quantity&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"])\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"except\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" KeyError:\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"&quot;Missing quantity&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"except\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" ValueError:\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"&quot;Invalid quantity&quot;\" class=\"string\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"77\" endIndex=\"85\" /><option startIndex=\"149\" endIndex=\"167\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"ValueError\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&quot;Missing quantity&quot;\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"TypeError\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>KeyError</code>, followed by <code>\"Invalid quantity\"</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Protect a port setting",
            "id": 152117,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What happens if <code>settings[\"port\"]</code> contains a value like <code>\"abc\"</code>?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"try\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  port = int(settings[\" /><text value=\"&quot;port&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"])\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"except\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" ValueError:\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"&quot;Invalid port&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" port\" /></content></code><selection multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">The function returns <code>\"Invalid port\"</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">The function returns <code>\"abc\"</code></item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">The function returns <code>0</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">The function returns <code>\"Invalid port\"</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Inside this function, what happens if <code>settings</code> has no <code>\"port\"</code> key?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"try\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  port = int(settings[\" /><text value=\"&quot;port&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"])\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"except\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" ValueError:\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"&quot;Invalid port&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" port\" /></content></code><selection multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">KeyError leaves the function because this handler does not catch it.</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">The function returns \"Invalid port\".</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">The function returns 0.</item><item value=\"4\" correct=\"false\">The function returns None after catching the error.</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">KeyError leaves the function because this handler does not catch it.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Check a focused handler",
            "id": 152118,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p><code>process_order()</code> can skip one order. Which design keeps the handler focused and lets unrelated failures surface?</p><selection multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Catch <code>ValueError</code> around quantity conversion in <code>process_order()</code>, then calculate and save outside the handler</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Wrap conversion, calculation, and saving in a bare <code>except</code> block</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">Catch every error inside the conversion helper and return <code>0</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Catch <code>ValueError</code> around quantity conversion in <code>process_order()</code>, then calculate and save outside the handler.</p></body></html>",
